# The talk of tools/remote_talk.py: two text front ends in a remote
# game, A at 127.0.0.1 and B at 127.0.0.2.
B> remote
B< Looking for boards
A> remote 127.0.0.2
A< hello 127.0.0.2 full
A> new w
B< game black
A< game white
A> e2e4
B< move e2e4

# A asks to take back e2e4, and B plays on, which refuses it.
A> undo
B< 127.0.0.1 asks to take back its move
B> e7e5
A< move e7e5

# So B's undo asks for its own e7e5 back, and A agrees.
B> undo
A< 127.0.0.2 asks to take back its move
A> undo
B< Taken back
B> c7c5
A< move c7c5

# A takes back g1f3, with B's agreement.
A> g1f3
B< move g1f3
A> undo
B< 127.0.0.1 asks to take back its move
B> undo
A< Taken back
A> b1c3
B< move b1c3

# A draw offered, and refused by a move, and by no.
A> draw
B< 127.0.0.1 offers a draw
B> b8c6
A< move b8c6
A< Refused
B> draw
A< 127.0.0.2 offers a draw
A> no
B< Refused

# A draw agreed.
A> g1f3
B< move g1f3
B> draw
A< 127.0.0.2 offers a draw
A> draw
A< result 1/2-1/2 agreed
B< result 1/2-1/2 agreed
